  "previous_goal_turn_classification": "Progress: inspected current retained evidence and source, identified the still-used Quinn runtime boundary; this turn implements and measures a new isolated treatment.",
  "treatment": "Experiment: explicit indexed connection-driver scheduling.\nBaseline: current HEAD rebuilt in the same isolated source directory and target directory before the candidate overlay.\nTreatment: replace one spawned Tokio driver future per connection with one concrete driver owner per application-runtime worker, indexed slots, reusable free slots, per-connection deduplicated wake tokens, and batched readiness service.\nKeep: existing quinn-proto state machine, protocol state, TLS/crypto, stream APIs and their shared-state mutexes, endpoint ingress thread, UDP implementation and buffers, packetization, congestion, ACK policy, timers, application tasks, output limits and frozen clients.\nNot the old FuturesUnordered grouped-opaque-future experiment. This changes the scheduler data structures but does not remove all synchronization or implement complete single-owner protocol state. Any conclusion is restricted to this treatment; no full-rewrite conclusion follows.\nEach shard services at most 64 ready tokens per poll. Connection event polling retains Tokio cooperative budgeting, now shared within that owner turn. This scheduler fairness change is part of the treatment and must be evaluated through workload/correctness results.\nAcceptance: record verified throughput/private-room-mixed component histograms and CPU; paced reliable and datagram controls; 100k ready/measured/retired RSS, setup/retirement, final gauges. Freeze sources and both images; reject rather than integrate a losing treatment. No hosted deployment.\n",
